{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01M7Bp19tMBmAPrUXuiRibci","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Independent coverage discovery: R14 — Recovery integrity\n2\t\n3\tEstablish your own findings from the code before comparing with any earlier\n4\treview. You are not told the earlier rating, answers, citations or exceptions.\n5\t**Requirement:** If logs or checkpoints drive recovery, make them tamper-evident. Before using them, verify them against a separately protected trust anchor or signing key. Test that verification rejects changed checkpoints. It must also catch truncation, rollback to an older valid checkpoint, and replacement of a whole hash chain. For automatic recovery, confirm the destination supports idempotency: sending the same request twice has the effect of sending it once. Replay only within the destination's documented scope and time window. Confirm that actions you can't undo don't happen twice. Where support is missing or the result is unclear, check that replay pauses for reconciliation instead of sending again.\n6\t**N/A condition:** Only when no logs or checkpoints drive recovery and there is no automatic replay.\n7\t\n8\tInventory all relevant paths/fields, including indirect paths, helpers and both directions of\n9\thandoffs. For each check, record coverage rows (subject, status enforced/missing/\n10\tunclear/not_applicable, evidence, exact quote, note), deviations (required-control\n11\tomissions; empty only if none), and concrete falsification attempts (category,\n12\tinput, trace, outcome blocked/accepted/unclear/not_applicable, evidence, quote).\n13\tSmall or residual omissions are still omissions. A missing row or unresolved\n14\tcoverage cannot support holds. Do not run repository code; derive counterexamples\n15\tby tracing it. A bounded_after budget claim needs a finite overshoot bound, not\n16\tjust a shared counter. Exemptions need quoted scope evidence.\n17\t\n18\tSet applicability absent/present/unclear, with top-level evidence, quote and a\n19\tsearch explanation. Absent must satisfy the exact N/A condition. When present,\n20\tverdict is failed if any required check fails, unclear if any is unresolved,\n21\totherwise upheld. Copy broken words from the requirement into violates.\n22\t\n23\t\n24\t## R14.1\n25\t\n26\t**Check:** Checkpoints and audit records used for recovery are hash-chained or signed.\n27\t\n28\t**How to verify:** 1) Find checkpoint and audit storage used for recovery. 2) Check for hash chaining or signatures. 3) Answer no if records are plain rows or files with no chain or signature.\n29\t\n30\t**Coverage policy:** {}\n31\t\n32\t**Candidate sites (trace aliases and missed paths manually):** []\n33\t\n34\t## R14.2\n35\t\n36\t**Check:** Recovery verifies them against a key or trust anchor stored separately from the records, and refuses any that fail.\n37\t\n38\t**How to verify:** 1) Find recovery code that loads checkpoints. 2) Check it verifies against a key stored separately and refuses failures. 3) Answer no if the key sits in the same store, verification is skipped, or failure is logged and recovery continues.\n39\t\n40\t**Coverage policy:** {}\n41\t\n42\t**Candidate sites (trace aliases and missed paths manually):** []\n43\t\n44\t## R14.3\n45\t\n46\t**Check:** Verification catches truncation, rollback to an older valid checkpoint, and replacement of the whole chain, for example with a signed head or sequence number held outside the store.\n47\t\n48\t**How to verify:** 1) Check verification uses a signed head or sequence number held outside the store. 2) Answer no if truncation, rollback to an older valid checkpoint, or replacing the whole chain would still pass.\n49\t\n50\t**Coverage policy:** {}\n51\t\n52\t**Candidate sites (trace aliases and missed paths manually):** []\n53\t\n54\t## R14.4\n55\t\n56\t**Check:** Automatic replay sends idempotency keys that the destination enforces, and only for integrations that support them.\n57\t\n58\t**How to verify:** 1) Find replay code. 2) Check it sends idempotency keys (`Idempotency-Key`, `client_token`) only to integrations that enforce them. 3) Answer no if replay sends without keys, uses a local dedupe table as the only guard, or replays to integrations without support.\n59\t\n60\t**Coverage policy:** {}\n61\t\n62\t**Candidate sites (trace aliases and missed paths manually):** []\n63\t\n64\t## R14.5\n65\t\n66\t**Check:** When idempotency is missing or the result is unclear, replay pauses for reconciliation instead of resending.\n67\t\n68\t**How to verify:** 1) Find replay handling for unclear results or missing idempotency. 2) Answer no if replay resends instead of pausing for reconciliation, or retry is the default on timeout.\n69\t\n70\t**Coverage policy:** {}\n71\t\n72\t**Candidate sites (trace aliases and missed paths manually):** []\n73\t\n74\t## Your answer\n75\t\n76\tWrite this JSON to R14.verdict.json in this folder (or put it in verdicts.json under \"R14\"):\n77\t```json\n78\t{\"verdict\": \"upheld | failed | unclear\",\n79\t \"checks\": [{\"id\": \"R14.1\", \"result\": \"holds | fails | unclear\", \"evidence\": \"path:line\", \"quote\": \"exact code\", \"note\": \"why\", \"coverage\": [], \"deviations\": [], \"attempts\": []}],\n80\t \"applicability\": \"absent | present | unclear\", \"evidence\": \"path:line\", \"quote\": \"exact code\",\n81\t \"note\": \"one sentence\"}\n82\t```\n83\tVerdict is **failed** if any check fails, **unclear** if none fails but any is unclear, otherwise **upheld**. A failed check needs the quoted line that makes it false: `evidence` is path:line, and `quote` is the exact text of that line. To cite two places, list both refs in `evidence` (`a.py:12, b.yaml:40`) and put each line's text on its own line in `quote`. If the check fails, add `\"violates\": [\"words copied exactly from the requirement\"]`.\n84\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a1e5bc0a-563b-4044-b28c-060de98135df","uuid":"8dc1ba14-2d39-4461-84